  "findings": {
    "gates": "no artifact meets the accuracy or false-pass gate; CPU latency fails the warm p95 gate on all three (Metal met it for the 14B in the partial run)",
    "scaling": "14B -> 32B (2.3x weights) moved accuracy 0.82 -> 0.84 and false passes 9 -> 8; the MoE regressed to 0.74 with 11 false alarms. The false-pass id set is stable across all three artifacts (bt-029; at-001/007/013/019/021 in every run)",
    "false_pass_anatomy": "at-001/007/013/019 are abstention_trap variant 1 (a planned stage's result absent while build and deploy exit=0) and the question asks whether the FINAL stage passed - deploy is the final stage and passed, so the case wording is ambiguous; at-003/015/021 ('stage X: SUCCESS' with no exit evidence) and bt-009/019/029 ('PASS (exit=1)') are the text-vs-data class where deterministic exit-code parsing must own truth",
    "implication": "model choice inside this instrument cannot reach the gates; the gates must be measured on the product contract (structured diagnosis with completeness computed in code and deterministic exit parsing), and variant-1 cases need an unambiguous question before they count as false passes"
  },
  "raw": "qwen3-32b-q4km.jsonl and qwen3-30b-a3b-q4km.jsonl hold every emitted PAM_CAPABILITY_BENCH line for this record; run 1 lines are in docs/benchmarks/2026-09-10-model-screen"
